---
description: Project privacy, local CCE/context-mode use and agent workflow.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) before working. Apply the physical skills in
`.agents/skills/`, especially `mac-helper`, `cce-maintenance` and
`agent-orchestration` when relevant. Use the project's native `make` targets.

Use local CCE for semantic repository retrieval and local context-mode (CTX) for
large output and session context. Confirm `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` equals
the MCP server's project before persistent operations. Never use another
repository's index or a remote analysis/embedding service. Never index secrets.
Process large data locally; return only the useful result. If transport is down,
report that limitation and use bounded local CLI output without claiming success.

Work inline by default. Delegate only with current explicit authorization. Keep
private project data local except for the assistant provider the user explicitly
selected for the session. Choosing this client is not permission for additional
providers, cloud workers, remote MCP services or credential access.

Before edits, write a change record with exact prior-state backups and guarded
rollback. Verify changed behavior and run `make verify`. Do not run cleanup or
connect to SMB servers as a test. See [client setup](../../docs/agent-clients.md).
